       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so the effects can last a long time.\n\nTypical adult dosing:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily. 2.5 mg is used for frail or elderly patients or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg once daily.\n\nDid you mean 5 mg or 10 mg? If 50 mg is intentional, please tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with that noted. Otherwise, I'll enter the corrected dose as soon as you confirm."
